1
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:08,890
Unit 8, page 144 B1.

2
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:13,700
David is listening to a news report about floods in Bluefield.

3
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:18,360
Listen with him and complete the notes below.

4
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:23,810
There was a lot of heavy rain in Bluefield last week.

5
00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:26,730
The rain flooded many areas badly.

6
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:33,530
It destroyed more than 2,500 homes and many people were hurt.

7
00:00:33,530 --> 00:00:39,950
The heavy rain also caused big problems for many farmers in Bluefield.

8
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:46,630
John, a farmer living in Bluefield, said, This flood caused great harm.

9
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:50,120
The heavy rain washed away our crops.

10
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:53,640
We worked so hard all summer for nothing.

11
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,430
There is little for us to do.

12
00:00:56,430 --> 00:00:59,390
Everyone in my village is worried.

13
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:05,570
The government is doing everything to support the people in the disaster areas.

14
00:01:05,570 --> 00:01:11,740
Luckily, weather reports helped the government prepare before the flood came.

15
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:17,000
This means money and emergency workers are arriving quickly.

16
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,080
This gives the people in the disaster areas great help and hope.
